A||||6||Fleabitdog||88GT stalls in drive||||5||
Z||000000||Fleabitdog||10-24-2001||07:25 AM||||A couple days ago I drove my car(88GT, Automatic trans) for about 20 miles. Stopped at a red light car died. Starts right up but stalls when I put it in gear. After letting it sit awhile It ran fine for about another 15 miles. Then started running a little rough for about 1 mile, when I pulled in my parking spot it died. Started right up  but shuddered  when I put it in gear. I drove it yesterday for about seven miles no problem, but I beleive if I drove much more it would have done it again. I beleive it is heat related. Has 3/4 tank of gas in it. Any suggetions?||||reg||5
Z||000001||fieroluke||10-24-2001||07:50 AM||||Hi,<P>sounds like a bad TCC-Solenoid to me...<P>Best regards,<P>-Oliver||||reg||4
Z||000002||Raydar||10-24-2001||09:16 AM||||Yup. I second the TCC solenoid. Been there, done that. <BR>As a temporary measure, you can unplug the solenoid. It's a 4-prong square-looking plug on the front of the tranny, below where the front manifold connects to the Y-pipe. Your gas mileage will suffer, and your tranny will make more heat.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||88CoupeV6||10-24-2001||10:33 AM||||Hey fleabit, Miss all the fun we had at the dutch classic.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Yep, I also would say it is the TCC. I've never fixed one but it can be unplugged to stop the shutter.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||10-24-2001||10:51 AM||||I vote for TCC solenoid.  Been there done that.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jefrysuko||10-24-2001||11:17 AM||||Yep Tcc solenoid.  When you do yours you can come on over and do mine for me next.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fleabitdog||10-25-2001||05:25 PM||||Thanks everyone for your help. You all called it right. I unplugged the harness and no problems. One more question though. Can I drop the pan and get to the solenoid to replace it? Thanks  Dave||||reg||14
